- LocalizedText has NodeId 21 and typeKind UA_DATATYPEKIND_LOCALIZEDTEXT (20)
- ExtensionObject has NodeId 22 and typeKind UA_DATATYPEKIND_EXTENSIONOBJECT (21)

So a Variant with Type=22 will look up the ExtensionObject type (NodeId 22), and since its typeKind is UA_DATATYPEKIND_EXTENSIONOBJECT (21), the code path goes to the "extensionObject" case.

Now let me look at the full Variant decode flow again:

```c
DECODE_JSON(Variant) {
    ...
    /* Get the type from the JSON "Type" key */
    UA_NodeId typeNodeId = UA_NODEID_NUMERIC(0, (UA_UInt32)parseCtx->index...
    ...
    bodyType = UA_findDataType(&typeNodeId);

    dst->type = bodyType;  // Set to ExtensionObject type

    if(bodyType->typeKind > UA_TYPES_DIAGNOSTICINFO)
        return UA_STATUSCODE_BADDECODINGERROR;

    if(isArray) { ... }
    else if(bodyType->typeKind != UA_DATATYPEKIND_EXTENSIONOBJECT) {
        // Non-ExtensionObject scalar
        ...
    } else { /* extensionObject */
        DecodeEntry entries[2] = {{UA_JSONKEY_TYPE, NULL, NULL, false, NULL},
            {UA_JSONKEY_BODY, dst,
             (decodeJsonSignature) Variant_decodeJsonUnwrapExtensionObject, false, NULL}};
        ret = decodeFields(ctx, parseCtx, entries, 2, bodyType);
    }
    return ret;
}
```

